      "details": "One auditory inspection per nominal SOA and side pairing. The 40 displayed cells are an inspection grid chosen for this profile. The publication leaves exact Experiment 3 counts unresolved. Digital, stationary sound bursts and nominal order combinations only. The touch side and lead are annotations; there is no tactile output, independent masker, fixation-light hardware or response scoring. Auditory onset is scheduled from an implicit fixation at the row start. The toolkit SOA control measures a nonnegative delay from sound onset. Touch-first timing remains a planned value."
    },
    "implementation_gaps": [
      "The trial scheduler requires independent auditory and tactile triggers for signed temporal orders plus light feedback. This profile schedules only the auditory member of each pair.",
      "Speaker and tactile calibration must verify delivered intensity and acoustic-to-skin onset. Original waveform bytes and measured timing are unavailable.",
      "The tactile apparatus uses a two-site electrocutaneous stimulator with individual nonpainful calibration. The printed voltage range does not supply the pulse waveform, width or delivered current.",
      "Exact Experiment 3 per-block, per-cell and practice trial allocations are unreported. The inspection uses one auditory presentation per nominal cell."
    ]
